WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:03.780
Next question today is about the economy.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:09.419
David, how is Donald Trump still polling better
than Joe Biden on the economy?

00:00:09.419 --> 00:00:10.419
This is a really good question.

00:00:10.419 --> 00:00:16.720
And it gets to a lot of the way that Republicans
have operated for a very long time.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.230
You've got a recession going on.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:25.080
Trump is down eight, nine, 10, 12 points nationally
to Joe Biden.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.029
And yet he is still polling better than Biden
on the economy.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:32.430
Morning consult has Trump plus nine on the
economy.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.540
CNN has Trump plus 12 on the economy.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.540
You gov.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.500
Has Trump plus five.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.000
Quinnipiac says Biden is plus one on the economy.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.710
But that's way less than on basically every
other issue for Biden.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:49.400
Harvard Harris poll says Trump is plus 10
on the economy.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.530
So a couple of different things.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:53.140
Number one, the the lead is diminishing.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:58.840
So if you look at the trend line, Trump is
leading Biden by less and less on handling

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.710
the economy over time.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:06.821
There is a meme, there's a tendency to think
that Republicans are just better on the economy

00:01:06.821 --> 00:01:07.821
than Democrats.

00:01:07.821 --> 00:01:12.850
Now, the reality is that that's a historical
we did a analysis, we did an analysis earlier

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.710
this week about the stock market under Democrats
versus Republicans.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.000
Does far better under Democrats than other
Republicans.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.030
Unemployment tends to be lower.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:28.170
We've looked at all the numbers, but in practice,
Trump also doesn't know a damn thing about

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.450
the economy.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.380
Trump didn't know about currency valuations.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.820
He called Michael Flynn at 3:00 a.m. and said,
do we want a weak currency or a strong currency?

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:36.820
Which is good?

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:38.420
And Flynn said, talk to an economist.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.410
Trump has no idea on trade.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:45.110
Trump believes that the stock market tells
us how an economy is doing so.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:51.510
Part of it is that a lot of voters also think
those same things Trump thinks to figure out

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.710
how the economy is doing.

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:56.030
You look at the stock market, a lot of voters
think the same thing.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.240
And in fact, they tweet me all the time and
say the economy's doing great because the

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.140
stock market is doing great.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:10.349
A lot of what also needs to be considered
is that Republicans tend to do things economically

00:02:10.349 --> 00:02:12.560
that will have a short term focus.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.709
How many jobs can we create this month, even
though reopening early will hurt the economies

00:02:17.709 --> 00:02:18.720
in the long run?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.849
And a lot of the jobs jobs are crappy.

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:21.849
Right.

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:28.099
How many stock market points can we gain today,
even if it's with cash injections that are

00:02:28.099 --> 00:02:31.950
short sighted and won't really improve the
economy in the long run?

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.439
So that's a really important thing also to
consider, which is Republicans are far more

00:02:35.439 --> 00:02:43.099
likely than Democrats to do things that improve
the optics of the economy in the short term,

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:44.860
but don't really improve it in the long term.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:50.370
And this is where a lot of this translates
into the general belief that Republicans are

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.580
just better for your paycheck, you know, better
for your pocketbook or better for your bank

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:55.580
account.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:01.689
It's mathematically untrue, but unfortunately,
these, Meems, are pretty sticky.

00:03:01.689 --> 00:03:04.510
And just remember the fact stocks do better
under Democrats.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.950
Unemployment is lower under Democrats.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.480
Just about every economic indicator.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.189
We've looked at a bunch of others, although
I'm forgetting them now.

00:03:11.189 --> 00:03:16.260
They look better under Democrats and we shouldn't
allow them to take the narrative away.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.420
And the diminishing lead that Donald Trump
has on Joe Biden in terms of expected handling

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:25.249
of the economy is a sign that at least the
disastrous economic situation we have right

00:03:25.249 --> 00:03:27.730
now is affecting Donald Trump.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.230
We thought maybe he's Teflon, Teflon Don.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.269
Maybe nothing will affect him.

00:03:32.269 --> 00:03:33.269
Coronavirus.

00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:37.970
The subsequent economic collapse and his reaction
to the protests against police brutality have

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:38.970
hurt him very much.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:39.689
His approval down to 38 percent.

